            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A computing device (302) comprises one or more processors and is configured to operatively connect to and control a mobile defibrillator (AED) unit (306). The computing device is configured to perform a process and to detect a connection of the mobile AED unit and detect that one or more electrodes of the mobile AED have been connected to a subject. The computing device is further configured to receive EKG measurements of the subject recorded by the one or more electrodes, receive measured breathing data associated with breathing movements of a chest of the subject and analyze the breathing data to determine a breathing pattern of the subject. Analyzing the breathing data to determine the breathing pattern of the subject comprises modeling the movements of the chest, analyzing a breathing frequency, determining that the breathing pattern is a non-normal breathing pattern, and based on the determined non-normal breathing pattern, initiate a CPR protocol.</p>
            </abstract>
